"Coffee_Time_on_the_Rocinante" by "Zachary Geary"
"The Expanse - Coffee Time on the Rocinante" by Zachary Geary

[ --- THE MAP --- ]
[Floor 1]
The Bridge is a room. The description is "The nerve center of the Roci. Four crash couches face their stations in a semicircle, 
bathed in the glow of dozens of tactical displays. Above, the curved canopy offers a view of the endless black. The air smells 
faintly of ozone and recycled atmosphere. Everything here speaks to the ship's Martian military heritage - efficient, deadly, 
and built to last."

[Floor 2]
The Armory is below the Bridge. The description is "Weapon racks line the bulkheads, currently stocked with assault rifles, 
breaching charges, and vacuum-rated combat armor. The mag-lock strips are Martian Navy standard, still bearing the MCRN stenciling 
that no one's bothered to remove. A faint oil smell lingers in the recycled air."

The Airlock is north of the Armory. The description is "The primary airlock is all business - pressure indicators glow green on the 
inner hatch, and emergency vac suits hang ready in their alcoves. The outer door's viewport shows nothing but black and stars. Stenciled 
warnings in English and Chinese cover every surface, reminding you that space doesn't care about your mistakes."

[Floor 3]
The Third floor hallway is below the Armory. The description is "A narrow corridor with the ladder well running through its center. 
Doors to port and starboard lead to the med bay and lab. Handholds and foot loops dot the walls for zero-g maneuvering. The deck plates 
are scuffed from years of magnetic boot traffic."

The Med bay is west of the Third floor hallway. The description is "Medical equipment crowds the compact space - an autodoc dominates one 
bulkhead, its diagnostic displays dark but ready. Drawers are labeled in precise lettering: trauma supplies, pharmaceuticals, surgical tools. 
The antiseptic smell never quite fades. This is where the crew's been patched up more times than anyone wants to count."

The Lab is east of the Third floor hallway. The description is "Sample analyzers, spectrographic equipment, and a small centrifuge are mag-locked 
to the workbenches. This is Naomi's domain when she's running diagnostics or analyzing whatever strange thing the crew's stumbled into this time. 
Data screens flicker with readouts, and the organized chaos suggests someone who knows exactly where everything is."

[Floor 4]
The Fourth floor hallway is below the Third floor hallway. The description is "The main deck's central corridor connects the galley and captain's quarters. 
The walls show the wear of daily life aboard ship - handprints near the ladder, scuff marks at knee height, small dents from careless cargo handling. 
It smells like home, if home was a recycled-air tube hurtling through space."

The Galley is west of the Fourth floor hallway. The description is "The heart of the Roci's social life. A small table with mag-lock plates is bolted to the deck, 
surrounded by chairs that can lock down for high-g burns. The coffee machine sits like a shrine against one wall. Cabinets hold shelf-stable rations, spice packets, 
and whatever fresh food the crew managed to score at the last port. The air always carries a mix of synthetic coffee and recycled atmosphere."

The Captains Quarters is east of the Fourth floor hallway. The description is "Spartan even by Navy standards. A bunk mag-locked to the bulkhead, 
a small desk with a terminal, and just enough personal space to not feel like a coffin. The hatch seals tight - privacy is a luxury on a ship this size. 
A few personal items remind you this is home, not just a berth."

[Floor 5]
The Fifth floor hallway is below the Fourth floor hallway. The description is "Another deck, another hallway. The ladder continues its path through the 
ship's spine, with crew quarters to port and the equipment room to starboard. The lighting here is dimmer - no need to waste power where people just pass through."

The Crew quarters is west of the Fifth floor hallway. The description is "Bunks are stacked two-high along the bulkheads, each with privacy curtains and personal storage. 
The crew's personalized their spaces - photos, music players, books. It's cramped, but it's theirs. The air smells lived-in, a mix of different people making do in close quarters."

The Equipment room is east of the Fifth floor hallway. The description is "Vac suits hang in their lockers, helmets racked above. Emergency gear, repair equipment, 
and salvage tools are organized with Naomi's typical efficiency. Everything has its place and every place has its label. In an emergency, you don't want to waste time searching."

[Floor 6]
The Engineering shop is below the Fifth floor hallway. The description is "Machine tools, fabrication equipment, and spare parts organized in bins and drawers. 
This is where miracles happen - where Naomi coaxes broken systems back to life and improvises solutions to problems the ship's designers never imagined. 
The smell of machine oil and metal is strong here. The Epstein drive's thrumming is louder this close to engineering."

[Floor 7]
The Cargo bay is below the Engineering shop. The description is "The largest open space on the ship. Cargo containers are mag-locked to the deck in neat rows, 
though there's room for much more. The bay can depressurize for vacuum cargo handling - the massive outer doors are currently sealed tight. Supply crates from 
the last resupply are stacked against the aft bulkhead."

[Floor 8]
The Reactor core is below the Cargo bay. The description is "The Epstein drive's reactor hums with barely-contained power, its magnetic bottles holding temperatures 
that would make the sun jealous. Warning signs in multiple languages declare the radiation hazards. Shielding keeps the really nasty stuff contained, 
but you still don't want to linger here. This is the beating heart of the ship - the reason the Roci can burn like she does."

